diff --git a/docs/api/web-contents.md b/docs/api/web-contents.md
--- a/docs/api/web-contents.md
+++ b/docs/api/web-contents.md
@@ -2421,6 +2421,18 @@ changes:
 Controls whether or not this WebContents will throttle animations and timers
 when the page becomes backgrounded. This also affects the Page Visibility API.
 
+<!-- fixme: placeholder copy -->
+#### `contents.setHidden(hidden)`
+
+* `hidden` boolean
+
+Hides or shows the page without a window, as switching tabs does: a hidden page
+reports `document.visibilityState` as `hidden` and can be frozen. If background
+throttling is off, a hidden page keeps painting. A page that is being captured
+in a way that keeps it visible, such as with the DevTools Protocol's
+`Emulation.setFocusEmulationEnabled`, stays visible. The next visibility change
+of the owning window overrides this.
+
 #### `contents.getType()`
 
 Returns `string` - the type of the webContent. Can be `backgroundPage`, `window`, `browserView`, `remote`, `webview` or `offscreen`.
